---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import fishing2005 from '../assets/images/site/fishing_2005.jpeg';
import deer from '../assets/images/site/deer.png';

const roles = [
  {
    org: 'CCT',
    logo: '/logos/cct.png',
    title: 'Senior Product Manager, Insight Cash',
    dates: '2026 — Present',
    note: 'Own product strategy for Insight Cash, the cage, vault, and revenue-audit product in CCT’s Casino Insight platform. Shaping how we use AI-assisted development while migrating a legacy WinForms application to a multi-tenant web app on AWS.',
  },
  {
    org: 'DoubleVerify',
    logo: '/logos/doubleverify.svg',
    title: 'Product Manager',
    dates: '2023 — 2026',
    note: 'Owned the strategy for a four-product advertising suite, grown from $39M to $50M in ARR. Took Attention Measurement for Marketplaces from first discovery call to GA.',
  },
  {
    org: 'Oracle',
    logo: '/logos/oracle.png',
    title: 'Product Manager, Moat',
    dates: '2022 — 2023',
    note: 'Replaced seven disjointed internal configuration tools with a single self-service interface, saving roughly 120 FTE hours a month.',
  },
  {
    org: 'Gravitate',
    logo: '/logos/gravitate.png',
    title: 'Founding Product Manager',
    dates: '2020 — 2022',
    note: 'First PM at a pre-seed startup; $0 to $1M+ ARR in under two years. Also the ML subject-matter expert behind its fuel demand forecasting and best-price purchasing algorithms.',
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Fisher Ankney is a product manager and builder in Boise, Idaho — a statistician by training who ships the code."
>
  <div class="page-intro title-only">
    <div class="page-title">
      <h1>About</h1>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      Most of my week is ordinary product work — discovery calls, roadmaps, pricing, launches — but I don't hand
      a problem to engineering until I've pulled the data myself and built enough of a prototype to know the idea
      holds up. AI-assisted development has made that loop fast enough to be the default rather than the
      exception, so what I bring to a spec review these days is usually a working thing, not a wireframe.
    </p>

    <p>
      That habit comes from the way I got here. I trained as a statistician: a master's from Oklahoma State, two
      years teaching stats to auditorium-sized undergraduate sections, and before that two years designing
      experiments and fitting models for the USGS. It means I can read the paper, check the math, and tell you
      whether a lift is real or an artifact of how somebody sampled. For the four years I spent in ad
      measurement that <em>was</em> the job, and it's no less true now that the product is a ledger which has to
      reconcile to the dollar.
    </p>

    <p>
      The upshot is that I can sit on either side of the table. At Gravitate I was the founding PM at a pre-seed
      startup and also its ML subject-matter expert, researching and coding the forecasting and pricing
      algorithms that became the product. At DoubleVerify I owned a $50M suite of advertising products and took
      Attention Measurement for Marketplaces from discovery through GA.
    </p>

    <p>
      These days I'm senior product manager for Insight Cash at CCT, where casinos run their cage, vault, and
      revenue audit. I'm shaping how we use AI-assisted development, migrating a legacy WinForms application to
      a multi-tenant web app on an AWS backend, and running discovery with casino accounting, finance, and audit
      teams across the country. If you're building something where the measurement is the hard part, I'd like to
      hear about it.
    </p>

    <p class="resume-line">
      <a class="button" href="/fisher-ankney-resume.pdf" download>Download my resume (PDF)</a>
    </p>
  </div>

  <section class="timeline-wrap">
    <h2 class="section-title">Where I've worked</h2>
    <ol class="timeline">
      {
        roles.map((role) => (
          <li>
            <span class="logo" aria-hidden="true">
              <img src={role.logo} alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
            </span>
            <div class="role-body">
              <div class="role-head">
                <span class="org">{role.org}</span>
                <span class="dates">{role.dates}</span>
              </div>
              <p class="role-title">{role.title}</p>
              <p class="role-note">{role.note}</p>
            </div>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>
    <p class="credentials">
      M.S. Statistics, Oklahoma State University — Outstanding Master's Graduate, 2020 · B.S. Geology c.
      Geophysics, Colorado State University — Honor Senior, 2016 · Pragmatic Institute PMC Level II
    </p>
  </section>

  <div class="prose">
    <hr />
    <h2>Away from the desk</h2>
    <p>
      Growing up in northern Michigan I was raised on a steady diet of hunting and fishing. My home town of
      Grayling boasts a rich outdoors heritage — it's where Fred Bear opened up shop in 1933, and 26 years later
      it's where Trout Unlimited was founded. Hell, even the ubiquitous Adams fly was invented just a few miles
      down the road on the Boardman River.
    </p>
    <p>
      My parents had me out in the field back before I can remember, a service that I will forever be grateful
      for. We would regularly fly fish our favorite stretch of the Au Sable just ten or fifteen minutes from our
      house nearly year round.
    </p>
    <Image class="photo" src={fishing2005} alt="Fishing as a kid in 2005" width={720} />
    <p>
      November 15th is a holy day for all in northern Michigan. School would always be closed for this, the
      opening day of rifle season. I took my first whitetail with my bow from a tree stand in the woods behind
      the house at 13, and occasionally I still make the pilgrimage back to hunt whitetails in the north woods
      because there's nothing quite like it.
    </p>
    <Image class="photo" src={deer} alt="Whitetails from the north woods in 2006 and 2023" width={720} />
    <p>
      The day after I graduated high school I moved to Colorado, calling Fort Collins home for the next decade as
      I focused on getting an education and a career. Unfortunately I left most of my hunting and fishing behind
      during this time, only taking the occasional day trip to fish the overcrowded Poudre River. In early 2022 I
      decided I'd had enough of that and moved to Boise — a city in a state I had never set foot in before. Since
      the move I've been making the most out of every season in this bountiful new home.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .resume-line {
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  .button {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.65rem 1.4rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--accent);
    color: #fff;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .button:hover {
    background: var(--accent-hover);
    color: #fff;
  }

  .timeline-wrap {
    max-width: var(--content);
    margin: 3rem auto 0;
  }

  .timeline {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .timeline li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 48px 1fr;
    gap: 1.1rem;
    padding: 1.1rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .logo {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 48px;
    height: 48px;
    margin-top: 0.15rem;
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
  }

  .logo img {
    max-width: 34px;
    max-height: 34px;
    object-fit: contain;
    filter: grayscale(1) contrast(0.85) opacity(0.78);
    transition: filter 0.2s ease;
  }

  .timeline li:hover .logo img {
    filter: none;
  }

  .role-head {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 0.25rem 1rem;
  }

  .org {
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .dates {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    color: var(--muted);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .role-title {
    margin: 0.1rem 0 0.4rem;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--rust);
  }

  .role-note {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.025rem;
  }

  .credentials {
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .photo {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    max-height: 420px;
    object-fit: cover;
    margin: 2rem auto;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
  }
</style>
